From: der-meddler <njilasalexander36@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: notify: ignore the usb_restrict kernel parameter

Samsung's bootloader appends "usb_notify_layer.usb_restrict=1" to the
kernel command line when it boots the recovery partition. With the stock
code the USB notify layer then refuses every USB event ("usb restrict
param is set, disable all USB operations", is_blocked() always true), so
the gadget binds to musb-hdrc but never connects: no adb, no MTP, no
sideload in TWRP.

Drop the two checks. physwizz's A137F recovery kernels carry the same
change, which is why official TWRP builds for a13ve have working USB.

Signed-off-by: der-meddler <njilasalexander36@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/notify/usb_notify.c | 10 ----------
 1 file changed, 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/notify/usb_notify.c b/drivers/usb/notify/usb_notify.c
--- a/drivers/usb/notify/usb_notify.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/notify/usb_notify.c
@@ -794,11 +794,6 @@ static void reserve_state_check(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	pr_info("%s +\n", __func__);
 
-	if (usb_restrict == 1) {
-		pr_info("%s usb restrict param is set, disable all USB operations\n", __func__);
-		return;
-	}
-
 #ifndef CONFIG_DISABLE_LOCKSCREEN_USB_RESTRICTION
 	wait_event_interruptible(u_noti->init_delay,
 		(u_noti->lock_state != USB_NOTIFY_INIT_STATE
@@ -2651,11 +2646,6 @@ bool is_blocked(struct otg_notify *n, int type)
 	struct usb_notify *u_notify = NULL;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	if (usb_restrict == 1) {
-		pr_info("%s cause:usb_restrict\n", __func__);
-		goto end2;
-	}
-
 	if (!n) {
 		pr_err("%s otg_notify is null\n", __func__);
 		goto end;
